WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Instructor] In this video,
we're gonna think about

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.410
what happens when we multiply

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:07.443
or divide by 10, 100, or 1,000.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.410
Let's just start with an example.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.410
Let's say we wanna figure
out what 237 times 10 is.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.840
Pause this video and see
if you can have a go at it.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.470
All right, well, one way to think about it

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:26.450
is this is 237 10s, so if
I put my place values here,

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:31.450
so this is the 1,000s place,
this is the 100s place,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.410
I'm just not writing it out
in words just to save space,

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.680
sometimes you'll see it written
out as the word thousands,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.930
and hundreds, this is the 10s place,

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.050
and then this is the 1s place.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.620
Well, if I were to just say seven 10s,

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.660
I would put the seven over there.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:51.950
If I were to say 37 10s, I
would write it like this,

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:55.520
because 30 10s is three 100s,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.360
and if I were to say 237 10s,

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.880
I would write it just like that.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.880
Because 200 10s is two 1,000s.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.080
And so what just happened?

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.410
Well, all of my digits
shifted one place to the left.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.830
So what used to be in the 1s
place is now in the 10s place.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:18.010
What used to be in the 10s
place is now in the 100s place,

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.323
and what used to be in the 100s place

00:01:20.323 --> 00:01:23.530
is now in the 1,000s place,
but what's in the 1s place?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.690
We have to put something in the 1s place.

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:28.670
Well, we no longer have
any 1s in this product,

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.010
so we would just put a zero there.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.953
So 237 times 10 is 2,370.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:38.960
Now, one way to think about it is,

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.580
when I multiplied by 10,
I really just shifted,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.950
I put a zero right over here
at the end of this number,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.220
but it's important to realize
that what really happened

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:49.690
is I shifted all my digits
one place to the left.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:51.480
But what if we were to go
in the other direction?

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.620
What if we were to take, I don't know,

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.850
450 and we were to divide it by 10?

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.320
Well, you can imagine if multiplying by 10

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.870
shifts the digits one place to the left,

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.290
then dividing by 10 is
going to shift the digits

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.020
one place to the right, and so we have

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.810
a four in the 100s place, we
have a five in the 10s place,

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.800
and we have nothing in the 1s place.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.160
And so what used to be in the 100s place

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.960
will now be in the 10s place,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.770
so I will put that four right over there,

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.250
and then what used to be in the 10s place

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.370
is now going to be in the 1s place,

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.900
so I will put that five over there,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:30.690
and we have nothing in the 1s place--

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.390
If we did, and this is a little bit

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.200
out of this video's purpose,
but you could start to think

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.050
what might happen if this was not a zero.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:44.050
But we have 450 divided by 10
is 45, and it is indeed 45.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.420
Now, another way to think about it,

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.230
other than the fact that
all of the digits shifted

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:51.567
one place to the right is that we removed

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:54.763
this right zero here
when we divided by 10.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:59.590
Now, let's extend that, let's
say that we had 359 times 100.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.310
Pause this video and see
if you can figure out

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.060
what that is going to be.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.510
Well, there's two ways that
you could think about it.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:14.000
You could just think of it in
terms of this is 359 hundreds,

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.830
so let's put some places here.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.754
So let's say this is the 10,000s place,

00:03:18.754 --> 00:03:21.204
this is the 1,000s place,
this is the 100s place,

00:03:24.223 --> 00:03:26.003
this is the 10s place,
and this is the 1s place.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.980
So if you were to say nine 100s,

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.410
you would go right over there,

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.760
if you were to say 59
hundreds, it would be like that

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.590
because 50 hundreds are five 1,000s,

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.237
and if you were to say 359 hundreds,

00:03:40.237 --> 00:03:43.237
well, 300 hundreds is three 10,000s.

00:03:44.677 --> 00:03:46.693
And of course, in this scenario now,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.230
you would have no 10s and no 1s.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.650
And so what we see happened is

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:55.430
all of the digits shifted
two places to the left.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:58.970
What was in the 1s place
is now in the 100s place.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.880
What was in the 10s place
is now in the 1,000s place,

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.130
and what was in the 100s place
is now in the 10,000s place

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:10.130
and so this product is 35,900.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.130
Now, another way you could think about it

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:17.130
is this is the same thing
as 359 times 10 times 10.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.460
And we already know that
every time you multiply by 10,

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.420
you shift your digits
one place to the left.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.990
So if you're going to
multiply by 10 twice,

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.880
you're going to shift all your digits

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.260
two places to the left, which
is exactly what happened here.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.330
So based on that, what do you think--

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.160
or based on everything we've looked at,

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.590
what do you think, if
I were to take 75,000

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:49.980
and I wanted to divide it by 100,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.510
what do you think this is going to be?

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:53.420
Pause the video and see if you

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.840
can work through it on your own.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.980
All right, well, we've already
seen if you divide by 10,

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.240
you shift the digits
one place to the right,

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.270
and dividing by 100 is
really the same thing

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.270
as dividing by 10 twice, so
we really just need to shift

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.060
all our digits two places to the right.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.940
So what used to be in the 10,000s place

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.900
is now going to go to the 100s place.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.300
What used to be in the 1,000s place

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.250
is now going to be in the 10s place,

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.220
and what used to be in the 100s place

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.870
is now going to go into the 1s place.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:33.390
And so what we are going to get is,

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.273
instead of seven 10,000s,
we're going to get seven 100s,

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.520
instead of five 1,000s,
we're going to get five 10s,

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:47.940
and then instead of zero 100s,
we will now have zero 1s.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.230
So this is equal to 750.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.510
Another way to think about it,

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.260
and we've talked about it
before, if you're dividing by 100

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:56.510
and if you have some of
these trailing zeros here,

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.550
well, then, you would remove two of these

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:01.170
right-trailing zeros,
but it's really important

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.430
to know why that happened.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:06.080
Now, you've hopefully seen a pattern,

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.690
so I'll ask you two more questions.

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:11.440
Let's say that someone were to
walk up to you on the street

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:15.790
and say, "Hey, you, what
is 164 times 1,000?"

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.577
and they were also to ask you,

00:06:22.577 --> 00:06:27.577
"What is 98,000, I'll
just say 98,000 divi--

00:06:28.957 --> 00:06:33.450
"I'll say 198,000 divided by 1,000?"

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.733
Pause this video and
see if you can do this.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.330
All right, you've probably
seen the pattern now.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.870
Just as multiplying by 100
was multiplying by 10 twice,

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:46.000
multiplying by 1,000 is
multiplying by 10 three times,

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.860
so this is equal to 164,
and I'll color-code this,

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:55.700
times 10 times 10 times 10,
so what we're going to do

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.990
is shift all the digits
three places to the left.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:04.880
So instead of 164, this four
is no longer in the 1s place,

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.530
it is now in the 1,000s place.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.270
It is now in the 1,000s
place, and that makes sense.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:13.560
If you take four 1s and
you multiply it by 1,000,

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.470
you're going to get four 1,000s.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:18.390
What was in the 10s place
is now in the 10,000s place,

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.896
and what was in the 100s place is now

00:07:20.896 --> 00:07:23.200
going to be in the 100,000s place,

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.070
and so, in order to represent this number,

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.170
I'll have to put something
in the 100s place,

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.690
we'll have no 100s now,

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:31.410
I have to put something in the
10s place, I have no 10s now,

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.210
and I have to put
something in the 1s place.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:36.900
So it's going to be
164,000, and once again,

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.650
that's consistent with the pattern we saw.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:43.080
We've added three zeros to
the right of this number.

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.940
So similarly, what's
going to happen over here?

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.100
Well, we're going to shift all the digits

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:52.640
three places to the right, so the one,

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.210
it's going to go one, two,
three places to the right,

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:58.350
so what was in the 100,000s place

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.310
is going to go into the 100s place,

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:03.030
what was in the 10,000s place

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.170
is going to go one, two,
three places to the right,

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:08.310
it's going to go into the 10s place,

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:12.420
and what was in the 1,000s place

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.540
is going to shift one, two,
three digits to the right,

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.180
it's going to be in the 1s place,

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.260
or another way to think about it

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.730
is when we divide by 1,000,
especially when we have

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:23.800
these three trailing zeros,
those are going to go away.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:28.800
So instead of 100,000 here,
this is just going to be 100.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.243
Instead of 90,000 here, or nine 10,000s,

00:08:33.243 --> 00:08:35.280
this is just going to be nine 10s.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.790
And instead of eight 1,000s,
this is just going to be eight,

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.903
so it's equal to 198.

